  "body": "What happens: the user hides the Stock row in the Browser tree (the hidden-eye icon). Then he starts Simulate. The viewport shows the tool, the fixtures and the axes. It shows no stock body and no voxel body. Nothing tells him why.\n\nExpected: the user sees why. For example, the playback bar or the viewport says \"Stock is hidden - show it to see the material removed\". Or the simulation draws the stock body whatever the visibility of the Stock row. The maintainer chooses.\n\nEvidence: the maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-22 with a screenshot of v0.25.0 (commit 7e2a8119): \"bug; P1; no visible voxel body during simulation\". He unhid the Stock row and the stock body appeared. The report was first filed as the reopened issue #2396, then closed. See the comment on #2396.\n\nDone means: a pin test shows that Simulate with a hidden Stock row shows the hint (or draws the body), and the text is plain English with no G-code word.\n\nFound while handling #2396. This is not a wrong-output defect: the simulation is correct once the stock is visible.\n",
